    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (where YY is the last two digits of the registration year, e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions and the existing `customerCode`/`namesakeCount` patterns.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **New function step** \u2014 `AssignMembershipNumber.java` reads the owner via `@Val`, computes `registrationDate.getYear() % 100` (zero-padded), and sets `membershipNumber = <customerCode>-M<YY>`.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted `assignMembershipNumber` (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `assignCustomerCode` and `assignNamesakeCount`, so both the customer code and the defaulted registration date are already present.\n\n3. **Domain model** \u2014 `Owner.java`: added the persisted `membershipNumber` field (`membership_number` column) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it into the generated `OwnerDto` by name, so no mapper change was needed.\n\n4. **OpenAPI spec** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO carries the field into the JSON response.\n\n5. **Schema + seed data** \u2014 added the `membership_number` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres), and appended a trailing `NULL` to the positional owner `INSERT`s in the hsqldb and mysql `data.sql` files (h2/postgres use column-named inserts and needed no change). This fixed an initial \"row column count mismatch\" failure.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` passing.",
